            "review_comments": [
                "Does the new pattern have better IL? It seems like leaving the actual `throw` at the end of the method as it was previously should be fine.",
                "It's shaving off one `throw` instruction, although interestingly the assembly is identical in this case:\r\n\r\nhttps://sharplab.io/#v2:",
                "OK; I suppose it makes sense to just keep the changes in this PR just for consistency and thus having to keep in mind only 1 pattern instead of 2.",
                "On second thought, the happy path does do an extra short jump in the IL, so in theory it could be slower. However, since the assembly is the same I think the changes are fine.",
                "> It's shaving off one throw instruction, although interestingly the assembly is identical in this case:\r\n\r\nThe assembly is identical since you have a throwing placeholder for the `TryGetSingle` method in your test. If you change the `TryGetSingle` method to do something useful, the assembly will be different for the two cases.\r\n\r\n> the happy path does do an extra short jump in the IL,\r\n\r\nThe JIT is smart enough to recognize always throwing paths and reorder the method blocks as appropriate."
